ui-view-forces = Forces
ui-view-forces-hint = Arrows for the belt's pull on the carriage, on the Z axis and on each motor pulley's shaft. Their length grows with the force's order of magnitude; the value is written at the tip.
ui-view-planned = Plan
ui-view-planned-hint = A ball where the plan has the tool now, joined to where the tool really is (with the deflections drawn larger, the drawn tool moves away from there). The gap, following error and deflections together, is drawn as many times longer as the deflections.
ui-view-exaggeration = Exaggerate deflections
ui-view-exaggeration-hint = How many times larger the 3D view draws what bends: the frame swaying and the Z axis leaning, and the gap to the plan. They are micrometres; 1 draws them as they are.
ui-view-load = Load
ui-view-load-hint = Colours each part by the tightest check of the analysed cycle that concerns it: the motors by their motor and drive checks, gearboxes and pulleys by theirs, the belt by the belt checks, carriage and Z axis by the guide checks. Parts no check concerns keep their colour.
ui-load-room = room
ui-load-close = within 10 %
ui-load-over = over
ui-view-mode = Mode
ui-view-mode-hint = Shows the machine swinging in its lowest mode at the planned pose, slowed down to about one swing a second so that the eye can follow; the label by the tool gives the true frequency. The swing grows with the exaggeration. The simulation waits meanwhile.
ui-view-mode-none = This machine, as configured, tells no mode to show (it may need the elastic effects switched on).
ui-view-mode-label = Mode
ui-view-tool = Tool view
ui-view-tool-hint = A small picture from in front of the tool, following it, in the view's bottom right corner.
ui-view-compare = Compare
ui-view-compare-hint = Runs a second simulation beside this one with the effect picked here switched the other way, drawn as a see-through ghost. It gets the same commands from now on: start the cycle or a move to see the two side by side. It ends when the machine or the config changes.
